---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import MeasureLaboratory from "../../components/visuals/MeasureLaboratory.astro";
---

<Base
  title="Measure in Motion — Visuals by Zuhaib Ul Zamann"
  description="Pappus's centroid theorems, live: drag the axis, draw your own region, and watch volume and surface area assemble from centroid travel."
>
  <section class="experiment-head">
    <div>
      <a href="/mathematics" class="label back">← Mathematics</a>
      <p class="label label--accent">Experiment M02 · Geometry</p>
      <h1>Measure<br />in Motion</h1>
    </div>
    <p class="lede">
      A fourth-century theorem that still feels like a magic trick: the volume
      of any solid of revolution is just the region's area times the distance
      its centroid travels. Drag the axis, draw your own region, and watch two
      independent computations agree in real time.
    </p>
  </section>

  <MeasureLaboratory />

  <footer class="source-note">
    <span class="label">Fine print</span>
    <p>
      Pappus's theorems require the axis to lie in the region's plane without
      cutting through it — the instrument refuses, visibly, when you break
      that rule. The washer cross-check integrates 400 horizontal annuli and
      knows nothing about centroids, which is why its agreement with
      A·2πd̄ is evidence rather than tautology.
    </p>
  </footer>
</Base>

<style>
  .experiment-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr minmax(19rem, 0.68fr);
    align-items: end;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 3rem 0 2rem;
  }

  .back {
    display: inline-block;
    margin-bottom: 1.6rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  h1 {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    line-height: 0.88;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 31rem;
    padding-bottom: 0.2rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .source-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 10rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    padding-top: 1.25rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
  }

  .source-note p { max-width: 43rem; }

  @media (max-width: 44rem) {
    .experiment-head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .source-note { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
